 you do anything with them aside from having Caine/Abel/whoever turn up and tell you. I guess you could just have some sect hold it as their belief... but then what does that really do?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508334-what-if-abel-was-actually-the-first-vampire#post1508334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A: &quot;And then <i>my</i> descendants will plague <i>your</i> descendants with misery and murder too!&quot;\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>As I understand it, Caine's descendants are often described as being wiped out by the flood. Like, we're supposed to be the descendants of the third brother, Seth. (Although, I gather they<br /> <br /> So is that just mission creep on Abel's part?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-14T03:35:07-07:00","id":1508349,"title":"","content":"Intriguing. \ud83e\udd14","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-14T10:06:44-07:00","id":1508366,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure there is a part in the new TMR book about Abelism, more specifically the believe that Abel was a progenitor to many clans. They believe it is their task by YHVH to kill Caine's decedents in vengeance against their first murderer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-14T10:52:56-07:00","id":1508369,"title":"","content":"Rad theory for a cult<br /> Caine was just the guy who won the first Jyhad. He devoured his way to godhood, killed every other vampire, and effectively erasing the past; then he got really bored and starting the cycle all again by embracing new generations. For all we know Caine might not have been the first winner, he could have been the second, the third, the fourth; The world seems infinitely old by human timescales. It's the destiny of vampires to devour eachother until there's only one... <br /> <br /> <br /> Generally speaking though<br /> -Such high level things never really make it into my games. At most I've seen someone use a 5th gen. <br /> -I feel most of my players don't buy into Genesis enough for me to really go hard with it. The first city/flood/first vampire things are cool and I'll happily use them with the appropriate amount of salt but I don't think Abel as the first vampire is much of a revalation compared to, say, the first city being a paradise and God is evil, or more shockingly for gothic punk fans: God is purely benevolent but not omnipotent and has done his best to rid the world of vampires, and all the parts where he's not so great in the books are pure Settite slander.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-15T05:45:28-07:00","id":1508431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508334-what-if-abel-was-actually-the-first-vampire?p=1508344#post1508344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's an interesting idea. There're plenty of interesting twists you could do with the story. The issue is how you do anything with them aside from having Caine/Abel/whoever turn up and tell you. I guess you could just have some sect hold it as their belief... but then what does that really do?</div> </div> </div> </div>Meeting the First himself, finding out at Gehenna, chat with one of the Fallen, going on an expedition to some recently discovered Noddist site looking for information to better master the Cainite condition and prepare against the Ancients in the FInal Nights and find that the evidence is spelling out something totally unexpected, add some mysterious visions and dreams...<br /> It doesn't need to be 100% convincing, there just needs to be enough to seed chaos amongst the Noddists.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As I understand it, Caine's descendants are often described as being wiped out by the flood. Like, we're supposed to be the descendants of the third brother, Seth. (Although, I gather they </div> </div> </div>Abel wasn't planning for a younger brother or a giant flood that wasn't on the agenda when he was murdered. Caine and Seth's bloodlines could also have intermingled in places during antediluvian times, perhaps Noah or his wife had some of Caine's blood in their veins. Furthermore, vampires will be vampires. Post flood, I don't think higher generations really care about the distinction, whether or not it exists; and perhaps Abel went really off script and was also jealous of the brother his mother and his god replaced him with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So is that just mission creep on Abel's part? </div> </div> </div>Pretty much. I'm thinking it started off with Cain continuing to be an unrepentant asshole, Abel getting increasingly angry and both becoming increasingly antagonistic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrNatas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508334-what-if-abel-was-actually-the-first-vampire?p=1508366#post1508366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure there is a part in the new TMR book about Abelism, more specifically the believe that Abel was a progenitor to many clans. They believe it is their task by YHVH to kill Caine's decedents in vengeance against their first murderer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which ones? Some of the 13, the Caitiff or is it a Nictuku-type deal?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508334-what-if-abel-was-actually-the-first-vampire?p=1508369#post1508369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rad theory for a cult<br /> Caine was just the guy who won the first Jyhad. He devoured his way to godhood, killed every other vampire, and effectively erasing the past; then he got really bored and starting the cycle all again by embracing new generations. For all we know Caine might not have been the first winner, he could have been the second, the third, the fourth; The world seems infinitely old by human timescales. It's the destiny of vampires to devour eachother until there's only one...</div> </div> </div> </div>I do have a fondness for the idea that the WoD sort of cycles through endings and renewals.<br /> <br /> Although this does give me the idea for another heresy where Adam and/or Eve were/are the first generation of vampires along with the entire antediluvian family from which the pale imitation that is the modern vampire descend. Perhaps humans are actually just the end result of the blood thinning enough - or else vampires uplifted primitive humanity in their image to be their cattle/servants (I am getting so many ridiculous vampire-supremacy cults to run with here...)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Such high level things never really make it into my games. At most I've seen someone use a 5th gen. </div> </div> </div>As far as I'm aware, 5th is the highest you can get RAW anyway, although I've often found that many VtM fans seem to shy away from lower generations as though other players might call the police on them for even thinking about those kind of games or something.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> all the parts where [God]'s not so great in the books are pure Settite slander. </div> </div> </div><s>Heathen.\u200b</s>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-15T07:09:12-07:00","id":1508440,"title":"","content":"RAW you're free to go down to negative numbers since 3rd and 2nd gens are so nebulous that it's hard to know is &quot;1st&quot; is really the actual 1st: though rules only exist for 4th generation unless there's some Augustus statblock somewhere I'm missing so once you do get down to 3rd how much blood you can hold and use per turn /what kind of disciplines you can master is really up to the ST. Of course if we use 5th edition you can only really starve to death at this level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-15T08:30:43-07:00","id":1508448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508334-what-if-abel-was-actually-the-first-vampire?p=1508440#post1508440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">RAW you're free to go down to negative numbers since 3rd and 2nd gens are so nebulous that it's hard to know is &quot;1st&quot; is really the actual 1st: though rules only exist for 4th generation unless there's some Augustus statblock somewhere I'm missing so once you do get down to 3rd how much blood you can hold and use per turn /what kind of disciplines you can master is really up to the ST. Of course if we use 5th edition you can only really starve to death at this level.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant &quot;if you want to play a low generation straight out of character creation&quot;, which I forgot to specify. Unless the ST handwaves the creation rules away, as far as I know lowest is eight unless you you take the merit from Elysium then the lowest becomes 5th. Attaining 4th or lower requires diablerie in game. Anything more requires homeruling, and I feel like when we get to storyteller fiat we've left RAW behind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-15T11:27:06-07:00","id":1508465,"title":"","content":"It would certainly turn the setting on it's head and I like it. You should try it out in a game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}